      {
        "id": 78048,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-04T21:21:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Call me old fashioned, but if he leaks anything at all, except by the rare accident, then he's broken the agreement he made when he became a playtester, and shouldn't be allowed to be a playtester.&nbsp; I'm not sure why that's a controversial idea.&nbsp; You seem to think that it's OK to consistently leak lots of little stuff as long as he doesn't leak something you consider big and important, and maybe that's a legitimite difference of opinion.&nbsp; But no, I don't think simply pointing out that a guy who violates the playtester agreement should probably not be a playtester is rude.&nbsp; That seems like common sense to me.&nbsp; I'm not trying to pick a fight with anyone.</p>",
